posts.body:
Oh! I've just recalled that the animation count advances by an extra 0.5 per frame when moving:
JavaScript:
Game_CharacterBase.prototype.updateAnimationCount = function() {
    if (this.isMoving() && this.hasWalkAnime()) {
        this._animationCount += 1.5;
    } else if (this.hasStepAnime() || !this.isOriginalPattern()) {
        this._animationCount++;
    }
};
I feel like this is probably the discrepancy you're seeing.
Note that if the character does
not
have "Stepping" animation enabled, then when they stop moving their pattern will reset instead (cf
updatePattern
).
As-is, Galv's plugin does not change this: moving still updates 50% faster. The value is evaluated when the character is assigned, so it can't vary as the character walks/dashes. Here's some untested plugin code in case you want to try to unify the cases:
Spoiler:
plugin code
JavaScript:
/*:
 * @target MV MZ
 * @plugindesc Character pattern no longer updates faster when moving.
 * @author Caethyril
 * @url https://forums.rpgmakerweb.com/threads/173421/
 * @help Free to use and/or modify for any project, no credit required.
 */
// Override - make move animation increment count by same amount as step.
Game_CharacterBase.prototype.updateAnimationCount = function() {
  if (
    (this.isMoving() && this.hasWalkAnime()) ||
    this.hasStepAnime() ||
    !this.isOriginalPattern()
  ) {
    ++this._animationCount;
  }
};
(Paste into a text editor, then Save As -> File Type: All Files, Filename: whatever
.js
. Then stick that in your project's
js/plugins
folder and import as usual.)
